## 🍳 2. Kitchen Set Requirements
- **Fully Black Glass Fronts**: All kitchen appliances (ovens, microwaves, hobs, and hoods) must be **fully black glass** with no visible stainless steel, chrome, or silver trim when closed/installed.
- **Induction Cooktops**: Hobs must feature standard **round induction coils** only (no flex zones or bridge zones), matching the family's preference for standard round cast iron and thick aluminum pans.
- **Dishwashers**:
  - Must be 60 cm fully integrated models.
  - Must have floor light indication: either a projection dot (**InfoLight**) or remaining time in minutes (**TimeBeam**).
- **Hoods**: Prefer manual/mechanical speed regulation (e.g. push-buttons or sliders) over automated wireless control (e.g. WiFi/Hob2Hood), as Hob2Hood automation is explicitly not desired.
- **Refrigerators (Liebherr Built-in Side-by-Side)**:
  - Large: **Liebherr IXRFS 5125 Plus** (500 L, Height 177 cm, BioFresh/NoFrost, ~9,700–11,336 BYN).
  - Compact: **Liebherr IXRF 4555 Prime** (374 L, Height 139.5 cm, BioFresh/NoFrost, ~14,887–16,417 BYN).


---

## 🧺 3. Laundry Set Requirements
- **Generation & Control Match**: Washing machine and dryer pairs in each set must be design-matched and generation-matched (sharing the same style and control panel layout).
- **Stacking Setup**: Dryers are always stacked on top of washing machines. The stack must specify the correct stacking kit (e.g., the **LG KSTK1** kit for LG pairs).

---

## 📊 4. Set Layout & Budget Sorting
- **Sequential Set Ordering**: Appliance sets must be named sequentially from left to right (Set 1, Set 2, Set 3, Set 4).
- **Budget Sort Order**: Sets must be sorted from left to right in **strictly descending order of their total budget**:
  - **Set 1 (Bosch Touch)**: Premium set (~13,883 BYN)
  - **Set 2 (Electrolux Touch)**: All-touch interface (~9,048 BYN)
  - **Set 3 (Bosch Manual)**: Balanced dials/LCD interface (~8,515 BYN)
  - **Set 4 (Gorenje Manual)**: Economy brand cohesion (~7,202 BYN)
- **Currency Format**: Always display prices and budgets in **BYN** (never use "rubles" or "р.").

